※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4205 LANG_TYPE_OPERAND_NOT_INTEGER

※ '&' works on the bits of a number and '∧' on truth values, and neither will
※ do the other's work.  C lets '&' take two conditions, which is usually a
※ mistake; here it is refused.
let ready: bool = true
let seen: bool = false

@[startup]
fn main() → bool:
    ready & seen
